From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lee Trager <ltrager@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 19:09:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: arm_mpam: Fix PCC channel lifetime during MSC
 removal

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167008

mpam_msc_drv_remove() releases the PCC channel before unlinking the
MSC from the SRCU-protected lists. If this drops the final channel
reference, an existing reader can dereference the freed channel through
its retained MSC.

Simply moving the release after mpam_free_garbage() is insufficient. A
concurrent garbage collector can claim the queued MSC and wait for the
grace period while the remove caller finds an empty garbage list and
releases the channel immediately.

Add an optional garbage release callback and use it to drop each MSC
PCC reference after the collector completes synchronize_srcu(). This
also releases PCC references when mpam_disable() destroys the MSCs.

Fixes: 0585297ee2e5 ("NVIDIA: SAUCE: arm_mpam: detect and enable MPAM-Fb PCC support")
Signed-off-by: Lee Trager <ltrager@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Seth Forshee <sforshee@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit b7436bb7ceb1262fcaed1d1f33c4b183f168613c https://github.com/NVIDIA/NV-Kernels/tree/linux-nvidia-6.18-next)
Signed-off-by: Lee Trager <ltrager@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Fenghua Yu <fenghuay@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>

Conflicts:
	drivers/resctrl/mpam_devices.c: this patch moves
	  mpam_pcc_chan_put() out of mpam_msc_drv_remove(); the early
	  return of the base for a missing MSC (284508da4e46) stays

Ledger-Change: C-02047
Ledger-Origin: nvidia-bos@2ccba858eef34a5780881588ed3a7a6a3997b023
---
 drivers/resctrl/mpam_devices.c  | 14 ++++++++++++--
 drivers/resctrl/mpam_internal.h |  1 +
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/resctrl/mpam_devices.c b/drivers/resctrl/mpam_devices.c
index 8005ef45821a..4f21bd8202ba 100644
--- a/drivers/resctrl/mpam_devices.c
+++ b/drivers/resctrl/mpam_devices.c
@@ -139,6 +139,13 @@ static int mpam_pcc_chan_put(struct mpam_pcc_chan *pcc_chan)
 	return -ENOENT;
 }
 
+static void mpam_msc_release(void *to_free)
+{
+	struct mpam_msc *msc = to_free;
+
+	mpam_pcc_chan_put(msc->pcc_chan);
+}
+
 /*
  * Number of MSCs that have been probed. Once all MSCs have been probed MPAM
  * can be enabled.
@@ -243,6 +250,7 @@ static LLIST_HEAD(mpam_garbage);
 static inline void init_garbage(struct mpam_garbage *garbage)
 {
 	init_llist_node(&garbage->llist);
+	garbage->release = NULL;
 }
 
 #define add_to_garbage(x)				\
@@ -263,6 +271,9 @@ static void mpam_free_garbage(void)
 	synchronize_srcu(&mpam_srcu);
 
 	llist_for_each_entry_safe(iter, tmp, to_free, llist) {
+		if (iter->release)
+			iter->release(iter->to_free);
+
 		if (iter->pdev)
 			devm_kfree(&iter->pdev->dev, iter->to_free);
 		else
@@ -2448,8 +2459,6 @@ static void mpam_msc_drv_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (!msc)
 		return;
 
-	mpam_pcc_chan_put(msc->pcc_chan);
-
 	mutex_lock(&mpam_list_lock);
 	mpam_msc_destroy(msc);
 	mutex_unlock(&mpam_list_lock);
@@ -2472,6 +2481,7 @@ static struct mpam_msc *do_mpam_msc_drv_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (!msc)
 		return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
 	init_garbage(&msc->garbage);
+	msc->garbage.release = mpam_msc_release;
 	msc->garbage.pdev = pdev;
 
 	err = devm_mutex_init(dev, &msc->probe_lock);
diff --git a/drivers/resctrl/mpam_internal.h b/drivers/resctrl/mpam_internal.h
index b594ee175cd3..fc4e46373952 100644
--- a/drivers/resctrl/mpam_internal.h
+++ b/drivers/resctrl/mpam_internal.h
@@ -56,6 +56,7 @@ struct mpam_garbage {
 	struct llist_node	llist;
 
 	void			*to_free;
+	void			(*release)(void *to_free);
 	struct platform_device	*pdev;
 };
 
